634
00:27:41.520 --> 00:27:42.980
This has been the hardest campaign

635
00:27:42.980 --> 00:27:45.180
the Army of the Potomac ever had.

636
00:27:45.320 --> 00:27:46.580
The second in the afternoon

637
00:27:46.580 --> 00:27:48.360
was the bloodiest part of the battle.

638
00:27:48.760 --> 00:27:50.740
At 2 p.m., they opened on us

639
00:27:50.740 --> 00:27:52.240
with over 100 cannon.

640
00:27:52.240 --> 00:27:55.060
We lay flat on our faces for two hours.

641
00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:58.380
The air was filled with shell bursting in every direction.

642
00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:00.800
The battery that lay in front of us

643
00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:03.100
had 55 horses and 80 men killed.

644
00:28:03.420 --> 00:28:05.060
That night and the next day,

645
00:28:05.280 --> 00:28:06.500
